 UnquotePath←{
⍝ Takes a path the way Git reported it and returns the path itself.\\
⍝ Git puts a path into double-quotes as soon as it holds a character that needs escaping, and
⍝ a blank is enough for that: `git status --short` reports "APLSource/Has Blanks.aplf". Note
⍝ that "core.quotepath=off" only stops the octal escaping of non-ASCII characters, not this.\\
⍝ Within the quotes Git escapes a double-quote as well as a backslash with a backslash, and
⍝ both come back unescaped here.\\
⍝ A path that is not quoted is returned untouched, so this can be applied to all of them.\\
⍝ Note that a rename, which Git reports as "old -> new" with each of the two paths quoted
⍝ separately, must be split by `HandleRenames` first.
     2>≢⍵:⍵
     ~∧/'"'=(⊃⍵),⊃⌽⍵:⍵
     '\\(["\\])'⎕R'\1'⊣¯1↓1↓⍵
 }
